The '''Western Plains''' ({{Langx|an|Planas Occidentals}}), alternatively known simply as '''Bayaran savanna''' ({{Langx|an|Sabana bayarana}}) are an extensive plain situated within the [[Baliscan Confederation]]. They are bounded to the northeast by the [[Matarrañya / Cañadapirén]], to the south by the [[Iarapema]] river and the west by the [[Salsipuedes Sea]]. The Plains cover more than {{Convert|203756|km2|sqmi|abbr=on}} and lies mostly in the [[Bayara|Bayaran]] community. Almost all rivers to the west of the Matarrañya drain westward through the Plains. These rivers have formed the [[Bayaran Delta]], an "arcuate" (arc-shaped) delta. Most of the delta is composed of {{W|alluvial}} soils made up by small sediment particles that finally settle down as river currents slow down in the estuary.

The soil has substantial amounts of minerals and nutrients, which is good for agriculture. Near the coast the plains are exceptionally flat and decline in elevation as they approach the delta and western coast of [[Atlántida]].  

Subsequent to the [[Colonial Balisca|Mesogean colonization of Balisca]], the area became accessible as a farming region. Grasslands made way for crop fields or were cleared and drained for settlement. Large areas are currently under crop cultivation, including wheat, maize, rice, sorghum, peanuts and sunflowers. Irrigated citrus orchards have been established. Several {{W|game farm}}s have to some measure reestablished the game diversity that existed here at the end of the 19th century. The Plains have been under threat in recent years from {{W|urbanization}} and proposed development of new [[Planned communities in Balisca|planned communities]] to alleviate [[Baliscan housing shortage|housing]] and land shortages in other areas of Balisca.

